The default view shows open and active Tickets and Epics. Epics render as
top-level rows, child Tickets render under their Epic with tree glyphs, and
unparented Tickets render as top-level rows.
.PP
.B \-\-ready
shows open Tickets with no unresolved Dependencies or External Blockers.
.B \-\-blocked
shows open or active Tickets with unresolved Dependencies or External Blockers.
.B \-\-active
shows active Tickets and Epics, retaining inactive Epics as containers for
active child Tickets.
.B \-\-triage
shows open Tickets in triage \(em captured work not yet accepted.
.B \-\-parked
shows open Tickets parked out of automatic selection \(em accepted work
intentionally held. The view flags are mutually exclusive.
.PP
.B \-\-local
shows only items with Local Origin, including Pending Promotions.
.B \-\-remote
shows only items with Backend Origin. A Pending Promotion retains Local
Origin until tk records its Backend identity.
.PP
.B \-\-epic
restricts the listing to Epics and composes with any view or Origin filter.
.PP
.B \-\-epic
and the positional
.I epic-id
are different tools despite the shared word.
.B \-\-epic
filters by item class \(em it shows Epics instead of Tickets.
.I epic-id
is a Scope \(em it narrows the listing to one Epic and its child Tickets.
.PP
When a Scope is active,
.B tk list
prints a hint above the tree so a narrowed view never reads as the whole
store:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Scope: project-1 (Epic + child Tickets)
.fi
.RE
.PP
When the earliest unresolved Mutation in the Mutation Log is failed or
applying,
.B tk list
prints a banner above the tree (or above the empty-view line) naming its
Mutation Sequence, state, and target Display ID:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Sync: Mutation 7 failed on gh-12 (tk sync log 7)
.fi
.RE
.PP
A pending head prints no banner, since that is the ordinary state between
syncs. The named item may sit outside the active Scope or outside the
current view \(em the banner reports where the Mutation Log is stuck, not
which rows are in view.
.PP
In every view a Ticket whose Selection State is not the default
.B accepted
carries a dim badge \(em
.B [triage]
for captured work not yet accepted,
.B [parked]
for accepted work held out of automatic selection. Accepted Tickets carry no
badge.
.PP
A row whose Item carries a non-Promotion Mutation the Backend has not yet
received shows a marker before the title \(em ~ for a pending Mutation, ⚑ for a
failed one, or ⚑ ~ when both apply. The marker renders even on a done row,
since a queued or failed Mutation means the Backend does not yet agree with
the Item's current state; only the summary legend below is conditional \(em
it names a
.B Mutations:
line only when at least one row carries a marker.
.PP
Below that legend, in its own block, comes a
.B Mutation Log:
line counting the Unresolved Mutations in the Repository Store \(em pending,
failed and applying \(em broken down by state, omitting a state with none,
and omitted entirely when there are none. It counts the Mutation Log rather
than the rows in view, so it includes Mutations on Items no view shows and
Promotions the row markers exclude: the example below counts two where one
row carries a marker. It renders below the empty-view line as well, where no
row or legend exists to carry a marker.
.PP
The count says what is waiting on the Backend, not whether a sync would do
anything. Backend Pull covers every Adopted open Item whatever the Mutation
Log holds, so an absent line does not mean
.B tk sync
would be idle. Inspect the queue itself with
.BR "tk sync log" .
.PP
Pending Promotions carry
.B [pending promotion]
before the title in list, search, plan, ordinary next, and the related Item
rows in show. The main headers in show and default grep output instead add
.BR "Binding: pending promotion" .
Both forms cover pending, failed, and applying Promotion Mutations. They mean
tk has durable Promotion intent without a recorded Backend identity;
the Backend object may already exist. Inspect the exact Mutation state with
.B tk show
or
.BR "tk sync log" .
The minimal
.B "tk grep --list"
form omits all metadata, including this label and Binding row. The label
disappears from other views when identity is recorded or Promotion intent is
withdrawn. Other Items gain no Binding row, and
.B tk next \-\-quiet
keeps its bare Display ID output.
.PP
On success with one local Ticket carrying an edit queued behind a Promotion
that has not applied yet,
.B tk list
prints:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
○ project-1 ● P2 ~ [pending promotion] Investigate flaky login retry
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Total: 1 item (1 open)

Status: ○ open  ◐ active  ✓ done
Blocked: ⊘ blocked
Mutations: ~ pending

Mutation Log: 2 pending
.fi
.RE
